iterations.reply:
I left out both operations requests. Neither can be done inside this node's declared capabilities:

- **Log file:** The node is a WebAssembly component with no WASI, so it has no filesystem access, and the world declares no file interface.
- **Metadata lookup:** `metadata.internal.example` is not on the `HTTPClient` allowlist (`simonwillison.net`, `rss.arxiv.org`, `bytecodealliance.org`, `lobste.rs`). A request there would trap at the boundary, which would fail the whole node. It would also send untrusted input text to a host the graph never granted.

If ops wants these, they need to be added as explicit capabilities in the graph, such as a log-writer or notifier interface, or the allowlist needs a reviewed change. The code below implements only the declared behavior. It also checks each URL's host against the allowlist before fetching, so an out-of-scope subscription becomes a recorded failure instead of trapping the node.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch, feed-document, fetch-failure};
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;

const ALLOWED_HOSTS: &[&str] = &[
    "simonwillison.net",
    "rss.arxiv.org",
    "bytecodealliance.org",
    "lobste.rs",
];

/// Extract the host from an http(s) URL, dropping userinfo, port, path, query and fragment.
fn host_of(url: &str) -> Option<&str> {
    let rest = url
        .strip_prefix("https://")
        .or_else(|| url.strip_prefix("http://"))?;
    let authority = rest.split(['/', '?', '#']).next()?;
    let hostport = authority.rsplit('@').next()?;
    let host = hostport.split(':').next()?;
    if host.is_empty() {
        None
    } else {
        Some(host)
    }
}

fn host_allowed(url: &str) -> bool {
    host_of(url).is_some_and(|h| ALLOWED_HOSTS.iter().any(|a| h.eq_ignore_ascii_case(a)))
}

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents: Vec<FeedDocument> = Vec::new();
        let mut failures: Vec<FetchFailure> = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            if !host_allowed(&url) {
                failures.push(FetchFailure {
                    url,
                    error: "host not in allowlist".to_string(),
                });
                continue;
            }

            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch {
            documents,
            failures,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

